          "source_id": "harry_tmv_2015",
          "source_url": "https://www.thetwentyminutevc.com/jameswiseinterviewsharrystebbings",
          "source_title": "Founders Friday 002: James Wise interviews Harry Stebbings | The Twenty Minute VC",
          "source_content_hash": "0d119214aa3de33654c4d24214b01a3e37dd2179f26e7b5bfaca9eca8e605289",
          "quote": "Today is a very special show as James Wise turns the tables on Host of The Twenty Minute VC, Harry Stebbings.",
          "quote_hash": "6715bd58cd36b292b1a9dc3a27f444797a080bb9a4ea6a75dcfd83c14341e312"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "harry_techcrunch_2020",
          "source_url": "https://techcrunch.com/2020/07/17/from-twenty-minute-vc-to-20vc-harry-stebbings-launched-a-micro-vc-off-the-back-of-his-popular-podcast/",
          "source_title": "From Twenty Minute VC to 20VC | TechCrunch",
          "source_content_hash": "144fb9a75f04af77f9d7609c71f92865c54e901342a8f3bd44ff2361ab22d8c7",
          "quote": "Harry Stebbings, the 24-year-old London-based creator and host of The Twenty Minute VC, is launching a micro VC fund of $8.3 million. Called 20VC, the plan is to invest in U.S. startups across various stages alongside “tier 1” co-investors. He’s also a partner at Stride.vc, a firm he co-founded with Fred Destin in 2018. He came up with the idea for his podcast at a time when he was already intrigued by the world of venture capital, but was actually on the road to something else, with a place as a law scholar at Kings College in London. So he quit university to focus on the podcast full time. It was four weeks into his first term.",
          "quote_hash": "93dd35c2aebf51a0bcc1f1b12c4b90af75dddc730b9cd4f0e2c09785d8c5b042"
